so plenty of tournaments have been  canceled recently due to the global  pandemic it's just not  safe right now to have a bunch of sweaty  dudes packed into a convention hall  but what if i told you one tournament  said [ __ ] it to health and safety  guidelines and went  ahead with the event anyway and then  tried to cover up the entire thing  one recent cod land said that they were  going online  but footage leaked this past weekend of  players at the event  playing call of duty and that's when  everything exploded  so what happened did the event  organizers lie  did players just not listen to  instructions it's a confusing story that  i tried to get to the bottom  all right guys you know what don't at me  is it's our youtube news show where we  break down the biggest stories from  esports and streaming and if you like  that  i got good news for you we're going even  deeper now on twitch  so tune in every wednesday at 1 pm  eastern for our talk show clouded  and make sure you follow the channel so  you know exactly when we go live  so back on july 31st the american gaming  network was supposed to host the agn  call of duty indianapolis open lan event  it was being promoted as one of the  biggest amateur cod events out there  with a prize pool of 7 500  to be clear this tournament was not a  part of challenger's league which is the  official semi-pro league of cod esports  agn is a party tournament organizer who  according to their website runs  tournaments for call of duty  valeran and rainbow six siege now as you  can imagine with the world in the midst  of a pandemic having a bunch of sweaty  dudes packed into a convention hall  is not the best look so on july 31st  the day the tournament was supposed to  start agn decided to move the tournament  online  quote after discussions with  representatives from activision we are  deciding to change the indianapolis open  to be online only for health and safety  concerns  players are advised to participate in  the tournament from their home location  alone we apologize for any inconvenience  in which this may bring upon players  spectators and organizations we look  forward to working with activision for  future events  end quote this sentiment was repeated on  august 1st by jeffrey elliott who  according to agn's website is the cfo of  the company  and while that sounds like the obvious  and smart thing to do  the tournament allegedly continued as a  lan event later that same day  basically what you just saw looks like  that lan event with a bunch of sweaty  dudes packed into a convention hall  exactly what agn said they didn't want  to happen  on top of that another video surfaced  that looks like a bunch of people  packed into an airbnb trying to continue  playing the tournament online  gage cash a co-founder of agn who has a  name that belongs in mortal kombat  distanced himself from the event and  said that the indie open was to be  played  online period but according to a report  from dexter there were allegedly agn  employees at the event  despite agn saying they had nothing to  do with it  people were even alleging that agn only  put out that original statement to hide  from activision blizzard who are the  publishers of call of duty  the fact that this lan event was still  taking place  now this whole situation caught the  attention of dominique jeleno who's the  general manager for the toronto ultra  a pro call of duty team competing in the  call of duty league  she replied to a tweet with quote i  reported  everything to activision blizzard  absolutely stupid and i can't believe  that  they thought a they'd get away with it  and b be bold enough to post about it  end quote  former mlg event organizer adam apigella  even weighed in calling the situation a  disaster  i also reached out to cash elliott and  multiple sponsors  associated with the tournament cash told  me that the narrative online is full of  lies and isn't true  but didn't explain why that's the case  and  elliott just pointed me to a statement  that agn made after all of this  controversy popped off  quote in order to preserve the  competitive integrity of the online  tournament  we have decided to postpone the second  day of competition  to next sunday august 9th 2020.  due to an overwhelming amount of players  away from home with the inability to  play in a safe environment  we feel that this is the best way to  ensure that everyone is competing  safely and fairly the remainder of the  tournament end quote  also when i went back to gather more  information on the indie open  agn has deleted the page from their  website now even if players  ignored agn and cash's statements that  the tournament had been moved online and  even if agn had nothing to do with this  secret land tournament  the question i have is why did they wait  until the day of the event to move it  online  it's not like the pandemic caught  everybody off guard both the cod league  and the challengers league moved all of  their remaining tournaments online  months ago why couldn't agn do the same  and remember a representative of  activision reached out to agn  which according to their statement is  why they decided to move the tournament  online  and that's a pretty big red flag because  to me what that says is that agn was  fully prepared to host a pretty big lan  event in the middle of a pretty  dangerous public health crisis  and the only reason they didn't is  because activision well  stepped in and told them not to because  let's be honest when you plan to host a  lan event in the middle of a  giant global health crisis you are  putting people in danger  now i have no idea if agn is going to  take disciplinary action against the  players who did show up to this  secret tournament also cash who if you  remember is a co-founder of agn  retweeted somebody comparing the  multiple worldwide human rights protests  with these tournaments  implying that if one is allowed to  happen these tournaments should also be  allowed to happen  and yeah i don't know if that's it chief  if agn knowingly hosted this secret lan  event after saying it was going online  that's [ __ ] up and they put people in  danger and if that's the case  i hope activision blizzard takes action  against these guys  the first like few months of this  pandemic i was [ __ ] all over the  place  like mentally physically i was kind of  lost and  you know recently i feel like i finally  got my footing under me and i'm doing  better  and yeah but i'm still [ __ ] a little  loopy the last  this week has been um [ __ ] insane  short weeks like i said are  just not i don't like them i don't like  them

